      "content": "Those researchers often point to differences in average scores on certain personality inventories across different groups, suggesting these variations reflect adaptation to historical environmental pressures. They might argue that differing social structures or survival challenges in ancestral environments led to divergent selection for traits like high or low impulse control. These arguments usually frame the observed differences as measurable, albeit subtle, phenotypic expressions of long-term evolutionary divergence.",
